      "notes": [
        "Windows network columns now receive per-process TCP/UDP data from the Hoddmimis helper. The full MSI installs and starts it automatically. ZIP users run `Install-HoddmimisHelper.ps1` once from an elevated PowerShell, then launch Hoddmimis normally. Standalone TUI clients can use the same service. Totals start when the helper begins observing the process.",
        "Open-file inspection now uses the Windows and Linux helpers. Upgrade and restart the Linux helper to enable access across process owners. The helper returns file names and descriptors, never file contents. Windows protected processes can still restrict access."
      ]
